  "solution": {
    "text": "Electron density between nuclei increased during formation of BMO in <math><msub><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> .<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/102121.PNG\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 106px;\" /><br /><br />BMO is <math><msub><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">ψ</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">ψ</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mtext></mrow></msub></math> (Linear combination of Atomtextc orbitals) provides constructive interference.<br />While by distructive interference anti BMO <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>ψ</mtext> <mtext>A</mtext> </msub> <mo>−</mo><msub> <mtext>ψ</mtext> <mtext>B</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> formed.",
